                <pb facs="0751" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.1121 Kudrasheff, Alexander</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Swenson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Oslo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1926-11-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 22,
                        1926</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 21.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 903</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that in
                    compliance with the Department’s instruction No. 298 of August 26, 1926, the
                    case of Kudrasheff, Chevalier, and Kopman was taken up with the Norwegian
                    Ministry of Foreign Affairs, which promised to use its good offices with a view
                    to securing the release of the three Americans imprisoned in Soviet Russia.</p>
                <p>The Legation is now in receipt of the enclosed note, dated the eighteenth
                    instant, from the Norwegian Foreign Office, in which is transmitted a
                    self-explanatory excerpt from the report of the Norwegian Minister at Moscow to
                    his government in this matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurits S.
                    Swenson</hi></signed></closer>



